-- CA_0266_phase167_us_house_tn_ct.sql
--
-- Slot CA_0266 reserved via `npm run steward --prefix backend -- slot CA` (author: Chris Andrews).
-- No migration runner exists; this file records SQL applied by hand.
--
-- Phase 167 (post-primary reconciliation, 2026 U.S. House; taken over by Chris Andrews 2026-09-24), the
-- two largest remaining clusters: TENNESSEE (80 rows, CD1-9) and CONNECTICUT (22 rows, CD1-5). Same shape
-- as CA_0263 / 1853: result ('advanced' | 'not_nominated'), result_source, result_recorded_at,
-- last_verified_at; provisional_until cleared only where the race is complete (rule 5).
--
--   102 rows: 56 advanced, 46 not_nominated.   TN 46 / 34.   CT 10 / 12.
--
-- TENNESSEE — the Secretary of State's certified November list, "Candidates for United States House of
--   Representatives, November 3, 2026 General Election" (USHouse_Nov2026.pdf, 2026-09-03): 46 names, and
--   every one is one of our rows — no TN candidate is missing, so every TN race is cleared. The 34
--   not_nominated are primary losers, each with its 2026-08-06 DISTRICT TOTALS in result_source.
--   ⚠ CD-5 incumbent Andy Ogles LOST the Republican primary (Charlie Hatcher 36,546 / Ogles 32,096).
--   He keeps his seat until January; no office_terms row is touched and is_active is not written
--   (Phase 167 rule 7).
--
-- CONNECTICUT — 167-PROGRESS recorded CT as "attempted and abandoned: the canvass does not appear to
--   exist". It does: the SOTS Election Center (ctemspublic.tgstg.net; ctemspublic.pcctg.net redirects
--   there) serves both 2026-08-11 primaries as "Official Results" (760/760 and 323/323). Only three
--   congressional primaries were held: CD1 D, CD4 R, CD5 R.
--     CD1 D: Luke Bronin 29,219 (53.64%) / John Larson 18,221 / Gilchrest 4,468 / Fortune 2,568 — the
--       incumbent's defeat 167-PROGRESS reported from news is confirmed from the official record.
--     CD4 R: Michael Ted Goldstein 4,632 / Miressi 1,606.   CD5 R: Shea 10,261 / De Barros 2,411.
--   SOTS has published no 2026 candidate list (newest 2014); the November field is taken from the
--   official SOTS November 3 2026 sample ballots (19 towns posted, covering all five districts). Seven
--   rows are not_nominated only by absence from those ballots, with no primary loss and no withdrawal
--   document found (Rice, Irizarry, Cerreta, Perez-Caputo, Bueno, Taddeo-Waite, Botelho).
--   RULE 5 — three CT races keep provisional_until: the sample ballots carry a certified candidate we do
--   not have — CD1 Mary L. Sanders (Green), CD3 Thomas Egan (Independent), CD4 Benjamin Wesley
--   (Independent). CD2 and CD5 are complete and cleared.
--
-- NOT HERE: Arizona CD2 (1 row, Curtis Goodwin, sole Libertarian on the primary ballot per the
-- UNOFFICIAL results page; the certified canvass and November list sit behind 403 / Cloudflare) — held.
--
-- IDEMPOTENT: guarded on result IS NULL. Dry run: BEGIN; ... ROLLBACK; against prod, applied twice in one
-- transaction, then rolled back and re-read.
-- ROLLBACK (once applied): UPDATE essentials.race_candidates SET result = NULL, result_source = NULL,
--   result_recorded_at = NULL WHERE result_source LIKE '%Recorded by CA_0266 (2026-09-24).'; and restore
--   provisional_until = 2026-08-27 (TN) / 2026-08-12 (CT) on the rows it cleared.

